License obligations by category
------------------------------

* **Apache-2.0 (items 4, 5, 6, 10, 12, 14, 17, 18, 20):** retained notices
  must be preserved when redistributing those clones. This project does not
  redistribute them; if you vendor any clone, carry its `LICENSE` + `NOTICE`
  along unchanged.
* **MIT / BSD (items 2, 7, 8, 9, 11, 13, 15, 16):** copyright notices must
  accompany substantial copies; same policy as above.
* **Unlicense (item 19):** public domain; no attribution requirement, listed
  here for completeness.
* **AGPL-3.0 (item 3, MiroFish):** treated specially. **No MiroFish code is
  imported or linked into this package.** `providers/simulation.py` exposes
  `mirofish_service`, which only speaks HTTP to a separately-running
  MiroFish backend (`FLASK_HOST:FLASK_PORT`, default `:5001`). Running
  MiroFish as an independent service keeps this repository's own license
  unaffected; if you modify MiroFish itself, the AGPL applies to *that*
  deployment, so provide its source to your service users.

Runtime dependencies installed from PyPI (not vendored): `requests`,
`pydantic`, `numpy`, `scikit-learn`, plus lightweight upstream deps
(`simplejson`, `prawcore`, `pyOpenSSL`, `chardet`, `lark`, `tiktoken`,
`sentence-transformers`, `twisted`, `openai`, ...) required to import the
clones from source.

Data-source terms (Section 9 of the research dossier) - Jikan, Google
Trends, Wikimedia pageviews, YouTube, Reddit, and general web crawling -
remain the operator's responsibility at run time.
